---
<ContentLayout
  title="Website Audit Cost: AuditWeb Prices and Quote Checklist"
  description="AuditWeb website audits start at $297 USD for a basic scope and $997 for a comprehensive scope. See what affects cost and how to compare quotes."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} toc={toc} showLeadForm={true}
  publishDate="2026-03-28" updateDate="2026-09-11"
>
<p>AuditWeb website audits start at $297 USD for a basic review and $997 USD for a comprehensive review. Large sites, migrations, multiple languages and complex architectures use a custom quote.</p>
<p>The final cost should follow a written scope. Compare the pages, data sources, manual checks, deliverables and follow-up instead of comparing price alone.</p>

<h2 id="our-pricing">What do AuditWeb website audits cost?</h2>
<p>AuditWeb publishes two starting prices and a custom option. Prices are in US dollars for every service area.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="AuditWeb website audit prices and scope">
<table><thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Starting price</th><th>Suitable use</th><th>Confirm before ordering</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr id="basic-audits-100-500"><td>Basic</td><td>$297 USD</td><td>Focused review of a smaller site or defined question</td><td>Pages, checks, report and delivery date</td></tr>
<tr id="comprehensive-audits-500-2000"><td>Comprehensive</td><td>$997 USD</td><td>Broader technical, content, competitive and experience review</td><td>Samples, data, deliverables and walkthrough</td></tr>
<tr id="enterprise-audits-2000-10000"><td>Custom</td><td>Quoted</td><td>Large, multi-site, migration or complex architecture</td><td>Limits, phases, stakeholders and dependencies</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Read the <a href="/website-audit-services/">main website audit service</a> page for current scope and terms.</p>

<h2 id="what-affects-pricing">What affects website audit cost?</h2>
<p>Cost rises with evidence and analysis effort. Page count matters but template variety, data preparation and manual testing can matter more than the raw URL total.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Question:</strong> one technical diagnosis needs less breadth than a cross-functional review.</li>
  <li><strong>Sample:</strong> more templates, journeys, countries and properties require more evidence.</li>
  <li><strong>Access:</strong> logs and analytics can require preparation, validation and secure handling.</li>
  <li><strong>Deliverables:</strong> reports, trackers, presentations and workshops require different work.</li>
  <li><strong>Follow-up:</strong> implementation, monitoring and re-testing are separate unless quoted.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="free-audit-options">What does the free option do?</h2>
<p>AuditWeb's free checker inspects HTML that you paste into the browser. It reports selected title, description, canonical, robots, H1, image-alt and viewport observations.</p>
<p>The <a href="/free-website-audit/">free HTML checker</a> does not fetch or crawl a live website. It does not measure live speed, SSL, accessibility or Google indexing. Use Google Search Console for first-party indexing and search-performance evidence.</p>

<h2 id="compare-quotes">How should you compare website audit quotes?</h2>
<p>Compare the same fields across every quote. A lower price may cover fewer pages, fewer review areas or a tool export without manual verification.</p>
<ol>
  <li>List the properties, page samples and user journeys included.</li>
  <li>Record the evidence sources and access the provider requires.</li>
  <li>Check whether every finding includes affected URLs and verification steps.</li>
  <li>Confirm file formats, meetings, revisions and implementation responsibility.</li>
  <li>Confirm price, delivery date, cancellation terms and data handling in writing.</li>
</ol>
<p>Review the <a href="/website-audit-services/report-example/">completed report example</a> to see what an evidence-based finding contains.</p>

<h2 id="roi-of-a-website-audit">How should you measure audit value?</h2>
<p>Measure audit value through implemented and verified changes. Record a baseline before implementation, track completed actions and compare the same search, performance or conversion definition later.</p>
<p>An audit does not create traffic or revenue by itself. Attribution also needs to consider releases, campaigns, seasonality and search changes during the measurement period. Do not treat an unsupported forecast as a guaranteed return.</p>

<h2 id="faq">What else affects the price decision?</h2>
<h3>Are the UK pages priced in pounds?</h3><p>No. AuditWeb's published starting prices are $297 and $997 USD across service areas.</p>
<h3>Does the price include implementation?</h3><p>No. Implementation requires a separate quote unless it appears in the written scope.</p>
<h3>Is a large crawl automatically a comprehensive audit?</h3><p>No. A crawl collects data. A comprehensive audit adds defined questions, validation, priorities and a usable handoff.</p>
</ContentLayout>
